🧠 Interview Follow-up (Very Important)

Suppose I ask you:

Why did you use partitioningBy() instead of groupingBy()?

What would you answer?

The expected answer is:

partitioningBy()	groupingBy()
Only for boolean conditions	For any type of key
Always returns Map<Boolean, List<T>>	Returns Map<K, List<T>>
Optimized for two groups	Can create any number of groups
Example
Collectors.partitioningBy(n -> n % 2 == 0)

Result:

{
    true=[2,4,6],
    false=[1,3,5]
}
Collectors.groupingBy(n -> n % 3)

Result:

{
    0=[3,6],
    1=[1,4],
    2=[2,5]
}

See the difference?

2 groups → partitioningBy()
More than 2 groups → groupingBy()
⭐ Remember Forever

If the classifier returns boolean, think partitioningBy(). Otherwise, think groupingBy().

